From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mostly_Harmless <geek520170@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:30:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] fix(xml): keep room for the terminator of a long tag

A tag of LABEL_LEN (10240) bytes or more filled label[] completely, and
the following '*labelPtr = '\0'' wrote one byte past the end of the stack
array (AddressSanitizer: stack-buffer-overflow). Recorder XML with a large
raw="..." attribute reaches this. Stop copying one byte earlier.
---
 src/XmlFile.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/XmlFile.c b/src/XmlFile.c
index 1ed424c..24dd4a0 100644
--- a/src/XmlFile.c
+++ b/src/XmlFile.c
@@ -203,8 +203,8 @@ int readXml(const char *const ipFile, DANMAKU **head, const char *mode, const fl
                 return 2; /* 读文件发生错误 */
             }
 
-            if (labelPtr - label < LABEL_LEN)
-            { /* label长度限制 */
+            if (labelPtr - label < LABEL_LEN - 1)
+            { /* label长度限制，保留结尾 '\0' 的位置 */
                 *labelPtr = ch;
                 labelPtr++;
             }
